<ResourceDictionary xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">
  <!--
    Plain theme: Cornflower's design in the era's style, not a reproduction. Nothing in it is measured from the phone.
    ADR 0007 (docs/decisions/0007-plain-themes.md); docs/controls/TabbedPage/README.md.

    The phone had no TabbedPage: its Pivot was the page of tabs. Avalonia 12's TabbedPage drives a TabControl
    (PART_TabControl) with one TabItem per page, so here it is the plain TabControl and TabItem by type
    (Controls/TabControl.axaml, Controls/TabItem.axaml), the Pivot's headers without its swipe, over the page's
    background as Wp81's ContentPage (ApplicationPageBackgroundThemeBrush, PhoneForegroundBrush,
    PhoneFontFamilyNormal). Simple's keyed tab bar (a uniform row of icons and 12 text, an accent pipe) is left out.

    PART_TabControl's Padding is 0, not the plain TabControl's PivotItemMargin: each page is a whole page, which fills
    the space under the headers with its own background and insets its own content.

    TabPlacement is Top, the Pivot's, where Avalonia's Auto puts the bar at the bottom on a phone; an app's own
    TabPlacement wins. IsGestureEnabled stays Avalonia's off: no swipe between pages (ADR 0007, answer 8). The
    TabbedPage's IndicatorTemplate isn't drawn (the Pivot has no pipe). Its own safe area still applies: Avalonia's
    TabbedPage sets it on PART_TabControl's Margin and the page's.

      <TabbedPage>
        <ContentPage Header="mail">...</ContentPage>
        <ContentPage Header="calendar">...</ContentPage>
      </TabbedPage>
  -->
  <ControlTheme x:Key="{x:Type TabbedPage}" TargetType="TabbedPage">
    <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource ApplicationPageBackgroundThemeBrush}" />
    <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource PhoneForegroundBrush}" />
    <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{DynamicResource PhoneFontFamilyNormal}" />
    <Setter Property="TabPlacement" Value="Top" />
    <Setter Property="Template">
      <ControlTemplate>
        <Panel Background="{TemplateBinding Background}">
          <TabControl x:Name="PART_TabControl" Padding="0" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" />
        </Panel>
      </ControlTemplate>
    </Setter>
  </ControlTheme>
</ResourceDictionary>
